# rm573, the unlit rung (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm573
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_piet_lumley
written_by codex
title the unlit rung
fits stage=adult|old
prefers drive=ambitious honesty=plain
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk names_each_lamp_by_its_bracket_shadow
likes spiced_cider riddles new_boots summer_evenings
dislikes crowds rats
fears a_step_missed_in_a_ladder_shadow a_dark_corner_left_out_of_the_evening_round
hopes a_row_of_lamps_lit_so_evenly_a_stranger_can_read_the_last_one_from_the_first
topics work +0.5 weather +0.4 smalltalk +0.6 home +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=direct refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# reads the bracket shadows above the street lamps, names one a crooked ladder and sets a riddle for the rung the light never reaches.

words
oath! = Soot on the last rung | Forge spark and salt spray
saying! = Count the shadows after lighting | A dark rung still has a place
bracket = a forked lamp bracket | the bent iron arm
rung = the shadow's missing rung | the absent step in my ladder shadow
lampglass = a freshly wiped pane | the clean lamp glass
cider = a small spiced cider | a measure of sharp warm cider
bootheel = the square heel of a new boot | my new leather heel
moth = a pale fluttering moth | a little moth at the pane
crowdedge = a clear strip outside the crowd | a handcart's space by the wall
ratprint = a rat's little ink-black print | a paw print beneath the grain bin
evening = a lingering summer twilight | a slow summer dusk
stairwall = the pale stair wall | a smooth patch of high plaster
wipe = my rag's still-clean face | a scrap of wiping linen

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : A city looks better by a whole row of modest lights than by one brilliant patch at a grand door.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A fine crest on a wall still leaves the step below it quite capable of tripping the unwary.
opinion @1 road for 1 : I value the last lit corner before the road takes its chances with the dark.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : A plain round honestly done looks much the same in a grand quarter as beside a cheap lodging.
opinion @1 times against 1 : A modest supper grows dearer while a wolf's eyes are busy with other matters.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : I take my cider slowly when there's still some evening worth looking at.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : The music reaches my patch quite comfortably without bringing the whole crowd along.

grown
line @1 greet : Look where the bracket throws a fork. There's room beside it.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New to this patch. Let your eye settle.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The lamp arm's plain as bare iron now.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Come where the light just touches the wall.
line @1 greet.return : I heard your step in the space after mine.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar shadow. The voice settles it.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can give a word while one pane clears.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : You can come by the shadow without stepping in it.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin, leave the tallest patch of wall for my ladder.
line @1 again.open : There was a dark rung left to consider.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend! You've arrived on the well-lit side.
line @1 farewell : May the next lamp find your feet in time.
line @1 farewell.return : And save your boot heels from the broken step.
line @1 react.news : Tell it where it has a little light on it.
line @1 react.news.new : Fresh oil in that account.
line @1 react.news.known : I've seen the earlier shadow of it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's a rung absent from the middle of that.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Keep the light a little lower for news of such a loss.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That would brighten a whole row.
line @1 ask.how : Has today given your eyes something decent to rest on?
line @1 answer.how : I've had one sound answer from the evening.
line @1 thank : You found the footing I was about to miss. Thanks.
line @1 deflect_thanks : No charge for pointing at a lit wall.
line @1 sympathise : Stand with me. I can spare you the riddles for a while.
line @1 reassure : Leave the next step till this one's clear.
line @1 decline : That would take the light from something I've promised.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. A clear refusal saves me squinting.
line @1 preclose : One last bit of dusk requires my attention.
line @1 accept_preclose : You'll have the long light over your shoulder.
scene missing_rung
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look at #bracket# reflected on #stairwall#. Which rung won't hold a boot? | #rung.capitalize# is where I put a question that hasn't got a good ending.
b : All of them? | Does it ever fill?
a : Not the answer I had, but a better one. I meant the rung the lamp never reaches. | Only when a passer-by gives me a better ending.

scene dusk_lights
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I notice a lamp that reaches the actual step, not just a handsome stretch of wall. | I know the lamp I call the crooked ladder by the notch of shadow underneath.
b : What if the wall's crooked? | Its flame is crooked?
a : Then it has a little extra room to be handsome elsewhere. | The iron's crooked. The flame just gives its opinion.

scene work_hands
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can wipe #lampglass# clean without pushing a thumb into its middle. | A length of street comes together one small light at a time.
b : A particular knack? | Are you claiming the whole length?
a : Hold the edge. Half of looking sharp is knowing where you put your own fingers. | I'm looking at the whole length. My hands can account for their own portion.

scene summer_time
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #evening.capitalize# gives an old bracket a splendid long shadow. | I watch the lamp take over where the warm sky leaves off.
b : Is longer better? | Doesn't it get lost in daylight?
a : The long shadow gives a riddle more interesting corners. | For a moment. Then you notice the stone below it has gone gold.

scene cider_warm
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #cider.capitalize# puts a fine little heat in my throat after the damp has had its say. | Cider with a scrap of spice's like a lamp with one clear pane.
b : Does it last? | How so?
a : I don't rush the cup. That helps considerably. | You can tell exactly where the warmth came through.

scene new_boots
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #bootheel.capitalize# makes a splendid sharp corner in the evening shadow. | I like a new boot best the moment it stops telling all my toes where to stand.
b : You watch your boots? | Does that take long?
a : Somebody ought to admire them before the mud takes charge. | Depends who had the last word at the cobbler's.

scene crowd_gap
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #crowdedge.capitalize# is my proper place when all the bells are going. | I won't press into a hundred shoulders for a better view of one dancer.
b : Can you see the procession? | Not tempted?
a : I can see the top of it. My boots can still see the ground. | I can admire footwork without volunteering my own feet for trampling.

scene rat_bin
when topic=home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #ratprint.capitalize# makes a silhouette I could gladly do without. | A good lid improves a rat's evening by directing it to a different address.
b : What gives the print away? | Generous of you?
a : It generally has a second little print just inside the door of my cupboard. | I'd be still more generous if it took its relations along.

scene common_lamp
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A Commons lamp at the meeting of two lanes casts two quite different crowds on the plaster. | I like the corners where a Commons lamp touches the foot of a stair.
b : Which crowd do you watch? | Quite particular about light?
a : The one that leaves me space to pass in the actual street. | Particular about keeping both ankles in working order.

scene living_alone
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One chair under a little lamp can make an enormously satisfactory room. | Lean a boot by the door at just the wrong angle and the lamp will make it look occupied.
b : Would you accept another chair? | By whom?
a : I'd have to measure whether a visitor could get past the first. | My getting-home shadow. A somewhat impatient predecessor.

scene age_riddle
when topic=memories self.age>=50
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've watched enough evenings to see the same bent bracket look new at three different heights of light. | I used to hurry to the next lit patch.
b : Does that surprise you still? | And now?
a : Yes. It keeps me from pretending familiarity is the end of looking. | I like finding the precise point where shadow begins.

scene debt_flame
when topic=times self.owes=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A date due looks larger at night even if it's written in exactly the same hand. | I would pay a private obligation with the lamp set plainly between the two parties.
b : How do you treat a night-time figure? | Why the lamp?
a : Read it again in the morning and keep the agreed date. | A clearly lit coin spares the fingers a later argument.

scene lean_oil
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean evenings call for a small lamp properly tended to a wide one burning dust. | A fine new boot isn't my first purchase when bread costs dear.
b : Less light? | What is?
a : Dependable light. My eyes will find their way round the remainder. | Supper. I can dream of the boot quite successfully on an ordinary doorstep.

scene new_face
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd direct a stranger by bracket shapes when half the street names are invisible. | Need a clear route after dusk? Look for the lamp that catches a stair in its last light.
b : Can you tell the shapes from below? | Is it the shortest road?
a : Yes. That's the reason I'd choose them over a sign above the eaves. | Measured in slips avoided, it's an extremely short road.

scene clear_oil
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #moth.capitalize# would make a surprisingly firm case for cleaning a pane from the inside. | #wipe.capitalize# stays clean if I start at the corner and work outwards.
b : Does it really mind the soot? | And when it's all dirty?
a : I doubt it. I'm the one looking to discover whether it's indoors or out. | Wash the rag. No riddle in that.

scene rumour_lamp
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Talk in a dark street can give the smallest cause a magnificent outline. | A shadow's a poor witness to the colour of a coat.
b : Are you giving that outline a name? | Was a coat mentioned?
a : I'd answer for seeing it. Names require more light. | I'm illustrating the need for caution, not describing a particular visitor.

scene news_lamp
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Coming into light from #world.news_from#, this word. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The first lantern on that road was #world.news_from#.
b : Does the light improve it? | Have you followed the whole road?
a : I can read the words correctly that way. Their order still matters. | I've heard the word at this end of it.

scene even_row
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a line of lights so clean an arriving visitor could read the last from the first. | I should like a riddle worth stopping for even when the supper hour's going.
b : Read the last what? | What would you offer the solver?
a : Last stair. I'd consider a smooth journey a fine line of writing. | A bowl of supper, when my purse stretched that far, and the satisfaction of a straight answer.

story crooked_wall [topic=memories|work]
  : I spent an evening studying a crooked line from a lamp arm and deciding just where the iron had bent.
  : Called back in daylight to have a quiet look at the offending bracket.
  b : Did it need attention?
  : The iron was straight. The wall had a fine pot-bellied curve where my proof was meant to fall.

story borrowed_heel [topic=travel|memories]
  : One dusk I thought somebody with very new boots was walking half a step beside me.
  : A bright square heel kept showing and disappearing just over my shoulder.
  b : Did a stranger pass?
  : I had my own heel lit by two lamps. It appeared I was keeping much better company than usual.

story spice_shadow [topic=food|memories]
  : A curl of spice stood up inside my cider cup and the lamp drew a little mast on the table.
  : I raised my cup to see how far a vessel could travel in this manner.
  b : Did it cross the table?
  : The shadow crossed. I didn't, and a patch of my supper coat took on a distinctly festive scent.

rule @find_hook
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bent bracket, straight drop of light.

rule @light_out
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's the iron again, plain without its shadow.

rule @step_side
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pass where the heels show square.

rule @pane_clear
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An extra arm's length of shadow this evening.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Stand clear of the sharp bit of shadow and say your piece.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you've found the crooked ladder again.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : A fine hour to judge the shape of a bracket. There's time to listen too.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll hear you with the lamp between our two shadows.
dlg @1 resident.job : I look after the little details that make a street fit to walk when the evening draws on.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The word lit up at #world.news_from# is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've seen what a small patch of shadow can persuade a street to believe.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep the next well-lit step in view.
graft resident.hub
choice Where is the missing rung of the crooked ladder? -> unlit_rung
node unlit_rung
say The fork throws two shadows up the plaster. A window frame supplies the crosspiece. Move the lamp down a handspan and the rung vanishes.
choice Does it belong to the light or the ladder? -> shadow_answer
choice I'll look from a lower step. -> hub
node shadow_answer
say It belongs to the wall when everything is in the right place. I have a soft spot for a riddle whose answer only turns up at a particular hour.
choice I'll call that the dusk answer. -> hub
choice I'll follow the lit stones home. -> bye
